course: dictionary
lesson: 15219
title: Septic: germs, tanks and slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Septic has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «The cut on his knee went septic, so it was red, swollen and painful.» Red, swollen and painful are the clues. Septic here means infected with germs.
explain: «Our house is in the countryside, so it has a septic tank in the garden.» Countryside homes often have a tank that breaks down waste. A septic tank is not a sickness, so do not mix the two meanings.
explain: Be careful with the slang meaning. «A septic» is an Australian or British slang word for an American, and it can sound mocking, so do not use it to tease people.
fact: Septic means infected with germs.
fact: A septic wound has gone bad: it becomes red, swollen, painful and full of pus.
fact: A septic tank is an underground tank where waste from toilets is broken down by bacteria.
fact: Homes not joined to the main sewers often use a septic tank.
fact: In Australia and the UK, «a septic» is slang for an American. It comes from rhyming slang, «septic tank» = «Yank», and it can sound mocking.
exercise: «The cut on his knee went septic, so it was red, swollen and painful.» What does septic mean here? | *Infected with germs | Cold and wet | Healed and clean | Covered by a plaster
exercise: «Our house is in the countryside, so it has a septic tank in the garden.» What is a septic tank? | A tank of clean drinking water for the kitchen | *An underground tank where waste is broken down by bacteria | A large pond for fish | A box for storing spare plasters
exercise: In health lessons, which phrase warns you to clean cuts and splinters? | a septic | septic and proud | septic tank | *go septic
test: «The septic tank under the field needs emptying every few years.» What does a septic tank do? | It keeps the field warm | It stores rainwater for the garden | *It breaks down waste with bacteria | It carries the post
test: «The nurse said the scratch might go septic if it is not washed.» What might happen to the scratch? | It might turn into a plaster | *It might become red, swollen and full of pus | It might grow into a tree | It might stop hurting straight away
exam: In Australia, «a septic» is slang: what does it mean, and why can it sound mocking? | A kind of rubbish bin | A polite name for a tourist | *An American, from rhyming slang «septic tank» = «Yank» | A doctor who cleans wounds
